Falsifies `manifest_note::verification::a_decoded_manifest_encodes_back_to_its_bytes`.

The defect: `decode` stops checking that the three bytes after the option letters are zero. Every
manifest then has eight spellings, and two readers could each be handed a different one of them.
The fields still decode correctly, which is why no host test built from real manifests notices.

Expected to fail: the assertion that `encode` of the decoded manifest is the descriptor again.

